# Cache policy. Added 30 Oct 2026, after pointing celebrateloop.com at this
# app served STALE /privacy and /terms from Cloudflare's edge.
#
# WHAT WENT WRONG. Neither this site nor the static one it replaced shipped a
# _headers file, so Cloudflare applied its own default to HTML and pinned it
# with `s-maxage=604800` — seven days. The moment the domain switched, the old
# static privacy.html and terms.html kept being served from the edge: /terms
# was two days stale, /privacy fifteen minutes. Those are the two URLs an App
# Store reviewer opens, and one of them was a policy that names neither
# OpenAI nor Uber.
#
# THE RULE. An HTML file at a stable path whose contents change on every
# deploy must be revalidated; a build asset whose filename contains a content
# hash can be cached forever, because a new build produces a new filename.
# Getting these the wrong way round is how a single-page app serves last
# week's page from a fresh deploy.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Vite emits index-<hash>.js / index-<hash>.css — the hash IS the cache key.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
